    "result_text": "I added both helpers to `hc/front/views.py`, and the pattern check found no high-severity deviations. I haven't run the Django tests.\n\n- **`_get_check_for_user(request, code, preload_owner_profile=False)`** loads the check by code. It returns `(check, rw)` and gives `rw=True` for superusers and project owners. For other users it looks up their `Member` row and returns that row's `is_rw`. If they aren't a member at all, it returns a 404.\n- **`_get_rw_check_for_user(request, code)`** calls the first helper and raises `PermissionDenied` when `rw` is false.\n\nThe helpers follow the `access.channel_for_user@v1` pattern, with the `# pcat:` marker kept above each one. They sit right above `_get_channel_for_user`. I added the optional `preload_owner_profile` argument because existing views already call `_get_check_for_user(..., preload_owner_profile=True)`. When it's set, the query also loads the project's owner and their profile.\n\nThe check reported two small deviations from the pattern, both because of that argument:\n- **PC107, medium:** the signature has one extra parameter.\n- **PC110, low:** the code has a small structural change.\n\nI didn't add any `pcat-allow` approval lines, so nothing needs human confirmation."
